1
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,440
(Coming up)
Can we eat now?

2
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:07,640
Let's have a little.

3
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:14,700
(Dig in!)

4
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,350
(Yang Glory arrives)
I'm here.

5
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,240
Come on, quick.

6
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:17,960
Fair warning,

7
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,320
this place is ruthless.

8
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:21,760
You snooze, you lose.

9
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:25,160
(Xin gets curious)
Is filming fun?

10
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,800
Modern-day shows are more fun.

11
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:28,480
Ning, you're filming one now, right?

12
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,400
Yeah.

13
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:30,920
So yesterday,
while we were working it all out,

14
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:32,360
you knew exactly what happened,
didn't you?

15
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:33,160
Right. Because imagine

16
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:35,680
(Inside Ke's head)
if I'd brought up the wire

17
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:39,000
coming through the back of the door,
I'd look suspicious.

18
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,840
How did you even think of that?

19
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:43,560
But when Ning says it,
he doesn't sound suspicious. See?

20
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:44,280
No.

21
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:47,000
He was trying not to spoil it for us.

22
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,800
(The killer takes notes)
Killer, got it?

23
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,600
I know you want this.

24
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:53,000
Isn't that kids' food?

25
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,160
(Big bro here)
You're younger.

26
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:55,560
(Got him)

27
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:57,760
(Just realized)
I'm the big sis now.

28
00:00:57,760 --> 00:00:59,360
I've somehow ended up on a show

29
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:00,560
where I'm the oldest one here.

30
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:02,160
Aren't you and Jin about the same age?

31
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:03,400
She's younger.

32
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:05,310
She still gives little-sister energy.

33
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:10,420
=Truth Supply Station=

34
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:12,140
(Case talk over, time to refuel)

35
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:14,400
(Jin's movie is out)
We'll see it and send you a selfie.

36
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:15,680
We'll get a selfie for proof.

37
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:18,240
Let's all meet up in Beijing
and go together.

38
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:18,600
Okay.

39
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:19,400
We'll send it to you.

40
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:21,440
We'll write you a whole review.

41
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:21,720
Right.

42
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:24,360
We'll make sure to rave
about the acting.

43
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,520
Are you posting it on Weibo?

44
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:26,240
WeChat Moments.

45
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:26,840
I'll post it on Moments.

46
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,840
Can I screenshot and post it on Weibo?

47
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:30,320
I'll block you first.

48
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,800
(Teasing Jin)
I'll make it private.

49
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:34,120
Hide it from her.

50
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,720
Hide it from you.

51
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:35,080
You won't see

52
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:35,600
what we post.

53
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:36,680
No, make it visible only to her.

54
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,320
She'll be the only one who can see it.

55
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:39,520
That works, too.

56
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:42,080
Wow, you're really shutting me out, huh?

57
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:44,620
(Just messing around)

58
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:46,760
I want broccoli.

59
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:48,200
(Broccoli fan)
I'm sitting here.

60
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,760
(Lotus root & pork rib soup returns)
There's lotus root, too.

61
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:52,440
I'm stealing a piece of broccoli.

62
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,240
I'm starving.

63
00:01:57,780 --> 00:02:00,300
(So good!)

64
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:04,680
(Sudden realization)
So you did have time to pull it off.

65
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,360
What are you even talking about?

66
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:07,620
You think it was me?

67
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:08,780
(Intense stare)

68
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:10,600
If you think it's me today,

69
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,520
Princess, you're way off.

70
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:13,920
Then who do you think it is?

71
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:15,080
I don't know.

72
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:16,400
All I know is, it wasn't me.

73
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,160
(Tempted)
Can we eat now?

74
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,240
Let's have a little.

75
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:28,300
(Dig in!)

76
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:29,980
(Keeping one eye on guard duty)

77
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:32,540
(Food, here I come!)

78
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:37,820
I'm seeing Bai in a couple of days.

79
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:38,980
(Where?)

80
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,280
At the Magnolia Awards.

81
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:41,800
He's going. He was nominated.

82
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,320
Have you seen him yet?

83
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,640
Not yet. In a couple of days.

84
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,420
(Photo already secured)
Oh, I see.

85
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:47,840
(Missing Bai)
I miss him so much.

86
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:49,560
Then go visit him on set.

87
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:50,680
I did last time.

88
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:51,360
I visited them

89
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:52,160
on "Live Up to Your Youth".

90
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,280
When?

91
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:56,480
During Chinese New Year,
when he was filming with Zhang Ruonan.

92
00:02:58,440 --> 00:02:59,640
Seriously, I cried.

93
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,840
And when he saw me,

94
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,320
(The best Bai)
he was really moved.

95
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:05,020
(Now he misses him even more)

96
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:07,220
(Ning Waver is here)

97
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:08,160
Sorry, Ning.

98
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,160
We were starving.

99
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:10,300
(Instant acting mode)

100
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,720
Ning, we already...

101
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:13,640
took one bite.

102
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:15,240
(Suddenly getting dramatic)
How could you do this to me?

103
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:16,720
Sorry, Ning.

104
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,200
I'm not eating.

105
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:19,880
You guys go ahead.

106
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:23,980
(Trying to stop him)

107
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,030
(Quick, calm him down)
Ning, wait!

108
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:25,640
Ning!

109
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:27,000
Ning!

110
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:27,640
Get on your knees.

111
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:28,520
I'm down.

112
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:31,380
(Gotcha!)

113
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,040
I'm kidding.

114
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:36,250
(Yang Glory arrives)
I'm here.

115
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,160
Come on, quick.

116
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:37,880
Fair warning,

117
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:39,240
this place is ruthless.

118
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:41,680
You snooze, you lose.

119
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,080
It's every man for himself in here.

120
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:45,840
The food isn't even all out,
and they're already eating.

121
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:49,320
Eat up.

122
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:50,060
(Nice)

123
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:51,660
(Yummy)

124
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:52,700
(Yum!)

125
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:53,940
(So good)

126
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:55,760
Food tastes better standing up.

127
00:03:58,760 --> 00:03:59,840
Why is it stringy?

128
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:01,600
Lotus root.

129
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:02,760
It's in both dishes.

130
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:05,680
So one gets stir-fried,
and one gets stewed.

131
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:06,760
That lotus root is working overtime.

132
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,000
They say

133
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,480
Wuhan lotus root is the best.

134
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:11,520
Dungeon glitch fixed.

135
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,520
Free meal unlocked in Dungeon 3.

136
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,320
Players may eat first.

137
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:18,320
Any stamina points gained
will carry over.

138
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:19,200
(Who found the meal card?)

139
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:19,920
No clue about the rest,

140
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:20,950
but we've got plenty of cucumbers.

141
00:04:20,950 --> 00:04:21,920
Hey, Zhou.

142
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:23,000
Give me that card.

143
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:25,700
(Holding Ding's meal card for him)

144
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:27,840
(Ding Chengxin +100 stamina points)
I'm way too good to you,

145
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:28,800
Ding.

146
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:29,800
I'm not even keeping any for myself.

147
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,160
So are you buying me food or what?

148
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:31,920
What's mine is yours,

149
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:32,720
and what's yours is still mine.

150
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:33,880
Come on, Ding.

151
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:35,400
Let them find the evidence first.

152
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,080
(Ding Chengxin +100 stamina points)
We'll go when it's time.

153
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:39,080
I need to keep my bell with me.
If anyone tries anything...

154
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:42,640
I'll ring for my...

155
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:45,560
Can you stop messing with me?

156
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:46,160
(Ding Chengxin +100 stamina points)

157
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,200
There's another one here.

158
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,320
This one's new, too.

159
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:49,140
(She points, he fetches)

160
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:50,300
(Ding Chengxin +100 stamina points)

161
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,840
There's one under the chair.

162
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:52,880
Yeah, another one underneath.

163
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:54,200
And there's one here,

164
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:54,520
Zhou.

165
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:56,680
(Complains, but keeps helping)
I've really turned you into...

166
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:57,760
Zhou, there's another one here.

167
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:58,720
(Ding Chengxin +100 stamina points)
There's one behind this, too.

168
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:01,120
(Literally the prince's secret guard)
You're really bossing me around now?

169
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,400
Whose card are you using?

170
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,520
(Ding Chengxin +100 stamina points)
Mine.

171
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:04,800
Isn't there another meal card here?

172
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:06,500
(Ding Chengxin +100 stamina points)

173
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:09,900
(Jin Jing +100 stamina points)

174
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:10,420
(Dungeon 3, Case 2: Stamina Summary)

175
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:11,190
(Liu Yuning, Zhang Linghe, Zhou Keyu: 0)

176
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:11,900
(Jin Jing: 100, Ding Chengxin: 700)

177
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:12,560
(Stamina Summary)

178
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:13,130
(Liu Yuning: 180, Jin Jing: 200)

179
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:13,900
(Zhang Linghe, Zhou Keyu: 0
Ding Chengxin: 1,200)

180
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,160
Has "Overdo" gotten a release date yet?

181
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:18,480
Is that the one from those set leaks?

182
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,280
Yeah.

183
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,000
Those clips were intense.

184
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:20,640
I saw those clips

185
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,760
and thought they looked amazing.

186
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:23,160
Did you see the one in the water?

187
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,760
And the one where you smashed a glass
on the balcony.

188
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:25,510
(Coming soon: "Overdo")
On the boat.

189
00:05:25,510 --> 00:05:26,180
(Footage sourced online)

190
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,760
(Stay tuned)
At least we got great footage.

191
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,640
(Xin gets curious)
Is filming fun?

192
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:31,280
Modern-day shows are more fun.

193
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,160
Ning, you're filming one now, right?

194
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:34,880
Yeah, I'm on set.

195
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:36,280
Are you filming a modern drama?

196
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:37,280
Yeah.

197
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,720
It's basically a crime drama.

198
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:39,920
(Cool)
A crime drama.

199
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:41,920
(Coming soon: "Evidence")
I love crime dramas.

200
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:43,600
I kept thinking
about what you said yesterday.

201
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:46,160
You said in the group chat
that our analysis was really good.

202
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:49,800
Honestly, looking back, we crushed it.

203
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:51,520
Especially when...

204
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,530
(Abrupt topic change)
I realized you have a real talent.

205
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:56,120
You're great with timelines,

206
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,360
layouts, all that stuff.

207
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:57,960
Right.

208
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,120
He's really good.

209
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:00,400
Numbers, spatial stuff...

210
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:03,920
So this door
must've been shut beforehand.

211
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:06,960
I think we can work backward
from the victim's position.

212
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,140
Toad Skill.

213
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:08,890
He jumped here,

214
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:10,800
then walked here. Boom.

215
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,760
Took four steps over here,

216
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:12,680
farted,

217
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:13,400
then walked over here.

218
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:17,080
Right, over here.

219
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:18,780
(Approved)

220
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:21,180
What Ning is best at is reconstructing

221
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,200
(Sharp observer)
how the crime happened.

222
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,080
Right.

223
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,240
He's been good at that since Season 1.

224
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:24,880
Exactly.

225
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:26,400
The killer definitely didn't leave
this way.

226
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:27,520
If he did,
he couldn't have opened the door.

227
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,600
Could they do it without going inside?

228
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,560
He can!

229
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:36,200
Everybody has their thing.

230
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:37,160
I'm also curious

231
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:38,840
how you...

232
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:41,280
always manage to come up
with these wild theories...

233
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:42,730
(A Jin-ius insight)
Get them right.

234
00:06:42,730 --> 00:06:43,040
Exactly.

235
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:46,040
We've all had wild ideas before,

236
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:49,440
but they're rarely this accurate.

237
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:50,960
So yesterday,
while we were working it all out,

238
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:52,400
you knew exactly what happened,
didn't you?

239
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:53,440
Yeah, I knew everything.

240
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:55,000
So while you were all analyzing it,
I was...

241
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:56,280
I was thinking,

242
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:58,120
(Keyu hesitates)
should I...

243
00:06:58,120 --> 00:06:59,240
Jump in?

244
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,040
Right. Imagine if I...

245
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:02,560
(Inside Ke's head)
If I'd brought up the wire

246
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:05,880
coming through the back of the door,
I'd look suspicious.

247
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,720
How did you even think of that?

248
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:10,440
But when Ning says it,
he doesn't sound suspicious. See?

249
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:11,160
No.

250
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:13,880
He was trying not to spoil it for us.

251
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:15,680
(The killer takes notes)
Killer, got it?

252
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,160
Why are you laughing?
I wasn't talking about you.

253
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:20,700
(Super awkward)

254
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:22,200
That laugh was pretty suspicious, Yue.

255
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:22,640
Are you some kind

256
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,680
(Just curious)
of pro at these?

257
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,680
(Even more curious)
You play a lot?

258
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:28,480
Sometimes with friends.

259
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:29,480
But not that often.

260
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:31,800
Last time we played was years ago.

261
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:32,160
Remember?

262
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:32,480
Yeah,

263
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:33,320
we played once.

264
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:35,760
Usually we'd play
with Justin Huang and...

265
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:36,600
who else?

266
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:40,160
No, it was you and me in Changsha
or somewhere else.

267
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:40,840
Ning was there, too.

268
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:42,640
Right, and Lin Mo.

269
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,040
(Now she remembers)
Oh, right! We went to an escape room.

270
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:44,800
Just once.

271
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:46,360
I was scared out of my mind.

272
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:48,720
That was during Season 1.

273
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:49,360
Season 1?

274
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,320
Was it while you were filming Season 1,

275
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:51,160
or did you all go on your own?

276
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:51,960
Back then,

277
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:54,200
(Thinking back)
many celebrities were in Changsha.

278
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:57,160
Then one night, someone invited us...

279
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:57,880
I mean...

280
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:58,920
It was people from the production.

281
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:01,200
It was a little easier
to go out back then.

282
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:03,720
Not that easy.
We got spotted that same night.

283
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:06,000
We didn't want random dating rumors,

284
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,560
(Getting ahead of it)
so we posted on Weibo first.

285
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,360
We made it clear there were three of us.

286
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,160
All three of us.

287
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,940
You know what would hit right now?
Fruit.

288
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:14,800
(Was that subtle enough?)

289
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,530
(Ke's review)
So subtle, but not.

290
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:18,840
I didn't say anything.

291
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:20,240
I get it.

292
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:22,320
You want something sweet, right?

293
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:23,290
Ding,

294
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,820
(Ke on drink duty)
want something to drink?

295
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:26,160
Pour me some.

296
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:27,240
Sure.

297
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:27,760
Pour me some.

298
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,200
Okay.

299
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:31,320
That should be good for my bones.

300
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:35,480
It's fine. You're young.
Why worry about that?

301
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:37,760
(Bones take time to heal)
Young or not, healing takes time.

302
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:40,030
True. Eat more.

303
00:08:40,030 --> 00:08:41,880
Says the two people with bad backs.

304
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:44,620
(Completely out of strength and options)

305
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:46,500
(Take care of yourselves, everyone)

306
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:48,640
Why'd they only pick one detective?

307
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:50,120
Let me tell you
why there's only one today.

308
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,240
Here's what happened.

309
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,200
Jin, it's simple.

310
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:54,160
(Let Ke explain)
There's only one possibility.

311
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:54,480
They...

312
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:57,500
The production team thinks you're just
too good at this.

313
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:58,720
(Secretly pleased)
Exactly.

314
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,960
Really? Based on what?

315
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:00,820
Because of that thing...

316
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:01,920
(Selective amnesia)
we all forgot.

317
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:04,320
We all... I can't remember.

318
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:05,560
We couldn't solve a thing.

319
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:06,760
But apparently you're too good.

320
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:07,600
No, let me explain.

321
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:08,120
Let me tell you

322
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:09,320
what they were thinking.

323
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:10,840
Since she couldn't get the Golden Key,

324
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:12,600
they gave her a special...

325
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:13,760
a special role.

326
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:14,320
At least

327
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:16,440
(Just teasing)
it would put the spotlight on her.

328
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:18,720
Too bad none of us paid much attention
to her today.

329
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:20,840
(Ning teases again)
We're too important, right?

330
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:21,940
(Dessert incoming)

331
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:22,820
(Eyes locked on target)

332
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:24,760
They were worried we weren't full,

333
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:27,400
so they brought fruit to top us off.

334
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:29,880
You want one, don't you?

335
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:31,080
I know you want this.

336
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,480
Isn't that kids' food?

337
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:33,980
(That look says everything)

338
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:35,860
(Big bro here)
You're younger.

339
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:37,260
(Got him)

340
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:39,040
Right, you're the oldest in your group.

341
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:39,720
Yeah, I'm the oldest.

342
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:41,080
Who's the youngest?

343
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:41,960
Liu Yaowen.

344
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,720
Right.

345
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:43,960
What year was he born?

346
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:46,400
I was born in 2002.
Yaowen was born in 2005.

347
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:47,760
2005?

348
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:49,240
He was born in 2005?

349
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:50,120
Yeah.

350
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:53,040
Our company now has kids born in 2010.

351
00:09:53,040 --> 00:09:54,680
Even someone born in 2005 is 21 now.

352
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:55,880
Right.

353
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:57,880
(Just realized)
I'm the big sis now.

354
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,680
People used to call you Yue.

355
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:01,960
Now it's "Sister Yue".

356
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,480
Even the staff now...

357
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,680
The crew used to all be older than me.

358
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,080
Now I'm the oldest one in the room.

359
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:08,960
They all look so mature.

360
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,660
(Gen Z unlocks work life)
They're all born in 2002, 2003, or 2004.

361
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:13,160
(Ning has something to say)
Guys,

362
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:17,560
I've somehow ended up on a show

363
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:18,680
where I'm the oldest one here.

364
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:21,600
How can any of you say you're old?

365
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:22,880
I can't believe I'm on a variety show,

366
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:24,320
and I'm the oldest person.

367
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,960
Isn't that something to be proud of?

368
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:27,720
I just realized it,

369
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,880
and honestly, it's terrifying.

370
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:29,840
I've never done a variety show

371
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:30,720
where I was the oldest.

372
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:32,440
At least when Bai was here,
you had company.

373
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:32,880
Right?

374
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:34,520
Yeah, at least we had each other.

375
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:36,480
Aren't you and Jin about the same age?

376
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,720
She's younger.

377
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,640
She still gives little-sister energy.

378
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,520
She's wise beyond her years, though.

379
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:42,600
That's different.

380
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:45,600
Jin's mature. She really gets life.

381
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:46,840
I get life?

382
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:50,840
Your energy really doesn't match...

383
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:53,120
You mean I don't seem old?

384
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:55,280
I mean, not for someone your age.

385
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,840
(Sincere)
You're basically a teenager,

386
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:58,680
like an 18-year-old

387
00:10:58,680 --> 00:10:59,880
(Yue knows what to say)
who looks at the world

388
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:02,400
and is still excited about everything.

389
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:04,140
(Jin is delighted)

390
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:06,320
It's so pink. What is it?

391
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,680
A peach blossom pastry.

392
00:11:07,680 --> 00:11:08,480
No idea.

393
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:09,880
I'll give it a try.

394
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:12,080
It's rock hard.

395
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:12,960
It feels hard.

396
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,920
Lychee.

397
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:16,080
("Empresses in the Palace" superfan)
Like the snacks Noble Lady Chun loved.

398
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:17,360
Once I finish this, and...

399
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,200
(Curious)
Is it good?

400
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:22,320
Yeah. It has this...

401
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:25,480
artificial lychee flavor,

402
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,880
like lychee gummy candy.

403
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:28,320
It tastes amazing. Seriously.

404
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:30,720
Artificial...

405
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,760
Artificial isn't always an insult.

406
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:34,160
It has a vibe.

407
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,960
(Yue talks, Jin cracks up)
It has a vibe.

408
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:37,820
(Delicious)

409
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:41,160
Why did this shoot fly by?

410
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:42,420
Because you're having so much fun

411
00:11:42,420 --> 00:11:43,680
(Yue turns on the charm)
with me here,

412
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:45,640
so time really flies.

413
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,200
We mean this whole season.

414
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,760
(Yue is crushed)
Wow. Way to ruin it.

415
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:49,360
Killer,

416
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:51,240
(Something's off)
you're weirdly energetic today.

417
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:52,760
You're especially excited today.

418
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:54,020
(Jin, look at him!)

419
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,440
You're completely different
from yesterday.

420
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:58,200
(Used to it by now)
He says that about me every day.

421
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,480
Oh, so I'm the easy target now?

422
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:00,720
Really going for it?

423
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,280
(Hmph!)
Keep it up, and I'll fight back.

424
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,700
(Hehe)

425
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:06,640
Ding, try that artificial lychee pastry.

426
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:07,320
(Yue's pick)
It's good.

427
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:08,400
It tastes amazing!

428
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,800
(Playing along)
I'll try.

429
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,160
How is that artificial?

430
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,480
That was just how I described it.

431
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:15,480
It doesn't taste like an actual lychee.

432
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:18,120
It's like lychee flavor turned up
to eleven.

433
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,280
It tastes like...

434
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:19,920
Gummy candy.

435
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:21,280
Lychee gummy candy.

436
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:22,920
Like a fruity mooncake.

437
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,040
Want some blueberries?

438
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:28,360
Yeah, I'll have some.

439
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,600
Just admit you're the Prince
of the Li Kingdom.

440
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:32,160
(Blueberry fanatic)
I love blueberries.

441
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:35,960
(Carb crash)
I'm wiped. Food makes me so sleepy.

442
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:38,480
Then let's nap.

443
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:40,680
Let's start napping.

444
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:41,960
Dreams fix anything.
Maybe the killer will show up.

445
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,440
(New show title)
Let's Start Napping.

446
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:45,440
Makka Pakka.

447
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:46,400
(Starting the lullaby)
Upsy Daisy.

448
00:12:46,410 --> 00:12:47,600
Makka Pakka, moo.

449
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:50,080
What do you do for fun?

450
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:51,680
At home, I just lie around and scroll.

451
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:52,880
Otherwise,
I see what my friends are doing

452
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:54,480
and invite myself along.

453
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:55,120
I'm always down.

454
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:56,720
(Never kills the vibe)
Even at midnight, I'm still in.

455
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:58,200
Tongcheng Travel, just pack and go.

456
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,400
Absolutely.

457
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:03,080
Yue,
are you filming tomorrow's episode, too?

458
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,480
You'll be here tomorrow, right?

459
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,120
Yeah.

460
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:08,280
Tomorrow's the modern-day episode,
right?

461
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:09,080
Right.

462
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,000
I play the property manager.

463
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,680
Tomorrow I'm playing security guards.

464
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:16,640
(Ning's rapid-fire questions)
Who told you? How do you know? What?

465
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:18,080
Why are you a security guard?

466
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:20,440
Because the outfit
screams security guard.

467
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:22,480
The second I put mine on,
I'm the janitor again.

468
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:23,800
Isn't that a property manager?

469
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:25,560
See? It's different.

470
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:26,680
Isn't that basically the same thing?

471
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:27,960
(Promotion!)
Sorry, I'm SWAT.

472
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:30,560
We meant the outfit...

473
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:31,520
(Finally gets it)
Looks like a security?

474
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:32,440
Right.

475
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,960
You've got serious big-brother energy.

476
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:36,920
You don't seem like the youngest at all.

477
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:38,520
I guess.

478
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:39,160
I just remembered

479
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:40,720
that you're the oldest in your group.

480
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:42,360
I started too young.

481
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,040
Would you say you're mature?

482
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:45,360
Yeah, I'd say so.

483
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,280
That's a good thing.

484
00:13:48,780 --> 00:14:30,740
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(Viewing Calendar)

485
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:06,560
♪Come now, players all,
let the game of reason start♪

486
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:11,000
♪Unlock each hidden trial,
let courage spark the dark♪

487
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:17,180
♪Night falls slow, shadows grow,
the sleuth is lost inside the maze♪

488
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:21,400
♪Figures pass, lanterns sparse,
dark currents drift without a trace♪

489
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:25,170
♪Wind picks up, footsteps rush,
cold laughter swallowed by the dark♪

490
00:15:25,170 --> 00:15:29,280
♪Truth concealed, the night
stands still, and nothing leaves a mark♪

491
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:33,580
♪An unsigned letter, coded words,
the solvers gather one by one♪

492
00:15:33,580 --> 00:15:37,690
♪A broken game, illusion reigns,
who's hiding what they've done?♪

493
00:15:37,690 --> 00:15:41,330
♪Hushed voices, nerves on edge,
wrapped in smoke and mirrors still♪

494
00:15:41,330 --> 00:15:43,460
♪The next second, deeper riddles,
or the answer to the kill♪

495
00:15:43,460 --> 00:15:47,410
♪Every piece of truth
has finally come to light♪

496
00:15:47,650 --> 00:15:51,570
♪Unlock the mystery, turn the question,
let's begin tonight♪

497
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:55,930
♪Side by side, no holding back,
follow every clue to find the truth♪

498
00:15:55,930 --> 00:15:59,490
♪The story blurs like flowers in fog,
let's begin tonight♪

499
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:04,400
♪Search for the vanished cipher,
trace the proof, and face the sleuth♪
